  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe UI link on Windows and all platforms now verifies that the listening server owns the token before sending any tool calls:\n1. `crates/app/src/mcp/link.rs`:\n   - Added `token_proof(token, nonce, role)` using clean-room SipHash-2-4 to prove token ownership without transmitting raw tokens over the socket.\n   - Updated `hello_line` and `hello_matches` for mutual challenge-response verification.\n   - Added `pid_alive(pid)` using `OpenProcess` on Windows and `libc::kill(pid, 0)` on Unix.\n2. `crates/app/src/mcp/link_client.rs`:\n   - `open` generates a fresh nonce, validates the server's proof, and refuses unverified peers.\n   - `call` bounds answer line reads to 16 MiB (`MAX_LINE`).\n3. `crates/app/tests/mcp_live/ui_link.rs`:\n   - Added `false_server_on_stale_entry_is_refused_with_no_tool_calls_sent`.\n\n## Decisions\n\nRecorded in `docs/decisions/3874-windows-stale-link.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft_app::tests::mcp_live::ui_link::false_server_on_stale_entry_is_refused_with_no_tool_calls_sent`\n- `camcraft_app::tests::mcp_live::ui_link::the_link_folder_is_the_users_own`\n- `camcraft_app::tests::mcp_live::ui_link::the_link_file_follows_the_open_project`\n- `camcraft_app::tests::mcp_live::ui_link::a_wrong_token_is_refused_and_the_window_goes_on_serving`\n- `camcraft_app::tests::mcp_live::ui_link::bad_ui_arguments_are_usage_errors`\n- `camcraft_app::tests::mcp_live::ui_link::a_cli_call_with_no_window_says_so_and_exits_3`\n\nChangelog: UI link: verify token proof from window and bound line reads\nFixes #3874\n",
